Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 05:30:15 -0700
Subject: [Backport] CVE-2025-10201: Inappropriate implementation in Mojo

Cherry-pick of patch originally reviewed on
https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8235084:
Hold back payload bytes to allow handles chunking in ChannelPosix

Under Linux SOCK_STREAM sockets, sendmsg() calls transmitting ancillary
SCM_RIGHTS file descriptors must also send at least 1 byte of
non-ancillary payload data; otherwise, the kernel may ignore or drop
the ancillary file descriptors.

When a message contains >128 handles and requires multiple sendmsg() calls,
holding back at least 1 payload byte per future handle chunk guarantees that
every batch of descriptors is paired with non-zero stream payload data.
If a message's data payload is too small to provide at least 1 byte per
batch, WriteNoLock() safely returns false.

